    "body": "## Description\n\nCreate a `CONTRIBUTORS.md` file at the root of the repository that lists everyone who has contributed to HoneyBee Browser. This is a friendly, visible way for new contributors to make their first pull request.\n\n## Steps to Complete\n\n1. Create a file `CONTRIBUTORS.md` at the repository root.\n2. Add the following header (indented below so it renders as a code block):\n\n    # Contributors\n\n    Thank you to everyone who has contributed to HoneyBee Browser!\n\n    | Name | GitHub | Role |\n    |------|--------|------|\n\n3. Add one row for yourself with your name, GitHub handle, and `Contributor`.\n4. Commit with the message `docs: add CONTRIBUTORS.md`.\n5. Open a pull request.\n\n## Learning Outcomes\n\n- You will learn how to fork a repository, create a branch, and open your first pull request.\n- You will learn basic markdown table syntax.\n\n## Helpful Resources\n\n- [GitHub: Fork a repo](https://docs.github.com/en/get-started/quickstart/fork-a-repo)\n- [GitHub: Creating a pull request](https://docs.github.com/en/pull-requests/collaborating-with-pull-requests/proposing-changes-to-your-work-with-pull-requests/creating-a-pull-request)\n",
